1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,919
What's Today's Video About? A First Meeting Conversation

2
00:00:06,919 --> 00:00:08,419
Scene 1: First Meeting Conversation

3
00:00:08,419 --> 00:00:12,352
Nice to meet you. You're sitting next to me, right?

4
00:00:12,375 --> 00:00:15,041
Nice to meet you.

5
00:00:15,064 --> 00:00:20,040
Nice to meet you too. Pleasure to meet you.

6
00:00:20,063 --> 00:00:22,797
I'm Anna.

7
00:00:22,820 --> 00:00:25,153
I'm Kim.

8
00:00:25,176 --> 00:00:29,053
Where are you from, Kim?

9
00:00:29,076 --> 00:00:32,843
I'm from Seoul, South Korea.

10
00:00:32,866 --> 00:00:34,947
Seoul?

11
00:00:34,971 --> 00:00:39,012
It's such a lively and famous city.

12
00:00:39,036 --> 00:00:40,671
Yes, it is.

13
00:00:40,695 --> 00:00:43,428
Where are you from, Anna?

14
00:00:43,451 --> 00:00:48,251
I'm from New York, in the U.S.

15
00:00:48,274 --> 00:00:50,207
New York?

16
00:00:50,230 --> 00:00:53,030
It's a wonderful city.

17
00:00:53,053 --> 00:00:57,320
When did you come to Japan, Kim?

18
00:00:57,343 --> 00:01:01,343
I arrived last Monday.

19
00:01:01,366 --> 00:01:03,216
I see.

20
00:01:03,240 --> 00:01:07,773
Have you gotten used to life in Japan yet?

21
00:01:07,796 --> 00:01:10,796
Not really, no.

22
00:01:10,819 --> 00:01:14,788
Why did you come to Japan, Anna?

23
00:01:14,811 --> 00:01:19,345
I love Japanese culture and anime.

24
00:01:19,367 --> 00:01:24,636
I hope to work for a Japanese company in the future.

25
00:01:24,660 --> 00:01:27,155
That's an amazing goal!

26
00:01:27,178 --> 00:01:31,811
Did you study Japanese before coming to Japan?

27
00:01:31,834 --> 00:01:33,168
Yes, it is.

28
00:01:33,191 --> 00:01:36,757
I studied for about six months in college.

29
00:01:36,780 --> 00:01:41,025
How long did you study, Kim?

30
00:01:41,048 --> 00:01:45,782
I studied for about a year in my home country.

31
00:01:45,805 --> 00:01:48,045
That's impressive!

32
00:01:48,068 --> 00:01:52,401
Your Japanese is really good, Kim.

33
00:01:52,424 --> 00:01:54,358
Thank you.

34
00:01:54,381 --> 00:01:59,660
But listening and speaking are still tough for me.

35
00:01:59,683 --> 00:02:02,449
I'm a little nervous about speaking too.

36
00:02:02,472 --> 00:02:05,639
Let's do our best together from now on!

37
00:02:05,662 --> 00:02:07,029
Yes, it is.

38
00:02:07,052 --> 00:02:09,107
Nice to meet you.

39
00:02:09,130 --> 00:02:13,330
Do you have time after class today?

40
00:02:13,353 --> 00:02:14,686
Yes, it is.

41
00:02:14,709 --> 00:02:17,200
I do have time today.

42
00:02:17,224 --> 00:02:21,597
If you'd like, would you join me for lunch?

43
00:02:21,620 --> 00:02:23,420
Sounds great!

44
00:02:23,443 --> 00:02:25,576
Let's go!

45
00:02:25,599 --> 00:02:30,074
There's a delicious ramen shop near the school.

46
00:02:30,097 --> 00:02:32,165
Ramen?

47
00:02:32,188 --> 00:02:35,722
I love ramen!

48
00:02:35,745 --> 00:02:39,642
Then let's go together after class.

49
00:02:39,666 --> 00:02:41,000
Yes, it is.

50
00:02:41,023 --> 00:02:43,028
I'm looking forward to it!

51
00:02:43,051 --> 00:02:52,060
You can download today's video script from the description and top comment. Please leave a comment before downloading!

52
00:02:52,060 --> 00:02:53,560
Scene 2: First Day as a New Employee

53
00:02:53,560 --> 00:02:56,047
Good morning.

54
00:02:56,070 --> 00:02:58,604
Good morning.

55
00:02:58,627 --> 00:03:02,260
I'm Tanaka, the new employee.

56
00:03:02,283 --> 00:03:05,016
I look forward to working with you starting today.

57
00:03:05,039 --> 00:03:07,973
I'm Yamada.

58
00:03:07,996 --> 00:03:09,962
Nice to meet you.

59
00:03:09,985 --> 00:03:15,028
First, let me show you around our department.

60
00:03:15,052 --> 00:03:18,132
Sure, I'd appreciate that.

61
00:03:18,155 --> 00:03:21,689
This is the sales department area.

62
00:03:21,712 --> 00:03:25,245
Everyone here is really friendly and kind.

63
00:03:25,268 --> 00:03:28,635
This is such a bright and lovely office!

64
00:03:28,658 --> 00:03:33,738
Your desk is right over here.

65
00:03:33,761 --> 00:03:36,028
It's a bright spot near the window.

66
00:03:36,051 --> 00:03:37,617
Thank you.

67
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:41,097
This desk is so neat and tidy!

68
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:45,610
You have a computer and some stationery on your desk.

69
00:03:45,634 --> 00:03:49,109
Go ahead and turn on your computer.

70
00:03:49,132 --> 00:03:51,219
Got it.

71
00:03:51,243 --> 00:03:53,739
I've turned it on.

72
00:03:53,762 --> 00:03:57,329
The password is written in the document.

73
00:03:57,352 --> 00:04:00,485
Okay, I've checked it.

74
00:04:00,508 --> 00:04:03,543
I've successfully logged in.

75
00:04:03,567 --> 00:04:06,367
Great!

76
00:04:06,390 --> 00:04:09,556
Where are you from, Tanaka-san?

77
00:04:09,579 --> 00:04:13,179
I'm from Tokyo.

78
00:04:13,202 --> 00:04:14,873
I see.

79
00:04:14,897 --> 00:04:18,904
What kind of work did you do before?

80
00:04:18,928 --> 00:04:23,494
I used to work in design at my previous company.

81
00:04:23,517 --> 00:04:25,984
That's wonderful!

82
00:04:26,007 --> 00:04:31,174
Your design knowledge will definitely come in handy in this department.

83
00:04:31,197 --> 00:04:33,063
Thank you.

84
00:04:33,086 --> 00:04:36,185
I'll do my best!

85
00:04:36,209 --> 00:04:39,576
Oh, it's almost noon.

86
00:04:39,599 --> 00:04:45,165
Would you like to grab lunch together?

87
00:04:45,188 --> 00:04:49,322
Yes, I'd love to!

88
00:04:49,345 --> 00:04:52,878
There's a delicious ramen place nearby.

89
00:04:52,901 --> 00:04:54,668
Sounds great!

90
00:04:54,691 --> 00:04:58,257
I love ramen!

91
00:04:58,280 --> 00:05:00,747
Let's go!

92
00:05:00,770 --> 00:05:04,337
Sure, I'd appreciate that.

93
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:11,465
You can review today's video with the link in the description and top comment. *Note: The site may be removed without notice.

94
00:05:11,465 --> 00:05:12,965
Scene 3: Greeting Neighbors and Learning Garbage Rules

95
00:05:12,965 --> 00:05:18,731
Excuse me. I just moved into room 301 next door.

96
00:05:18,754 --> 00:05:21,821
Oh, hi there!

97
00:05:21,844 --> 00:05:24,538
Nice to meet you. I'm Tanaka.

98
00:05:24,561 --> 00:05:29,528
Nice to meet you. I'm Suzuki from room 302 next door.

99
00:05:29,551 --> 00:05:32,240
I look forward to working with you starting today.

100
00:05:32,263 --> 00:05:36,263
This is a small welcome gift for you.

101
00:05:36,286 --> 00:05:37,519
Please, take it.

102
00:05:37,542 --> 00:05:40,142
Wow, thank you so much!

103
00:05:40,165 --> 00:05:43,059
That’s very kind of you, thank you.

104
00:05:43,082 --> 00:05:46,886
Oh, it's just a little something.

105
00:05:46,910 --> 00:05:50,558
Um, may I ask you a quick question?

106
00:05:50,581 --> 00:05:53,515
Sure, what is it?

107
00:05:53,538 --> 00:05:56,212
Could you tell me about the garbage rules?

108
00:05:56,236 --> 00:05:58,602
Of course.

109
00:05:58,625 --> 00:06:03,425
Burnable trash is collected on Mondays and Thursdays.

110
00:06:03,448 --> 00:06:06,482
Mondays and Thursdays, got it.

111
00:06:06,505 --> 00:06:10,438
What time and where should I take it out in the morning?

112
00:06:10,461 --> 00:06:16,228
Please put it in the trash area downstairs by 8 AM, inside the net.

113
00:06:16,251 --> 00:06:18,133
Got it.

114
00:06:18,156 --> 00:06:19,956
Thank you.

115
00:06:19,980 --> 00:06:24,180
Plastic bottles and cans are collected on Wednesdays.

116
00:06:24,203 --> 00:06:26,042
Wednesdays, I see.

117
00:06:26,065 --> 00:06:28,632
I'll remember that.

118
00:06:28,655 --> 00:06:33,188
By the way, could you tell me how to get to the station?

119
00:06:33,211 --> 00:06:35,578
Sure, to the station, right?

120
00:06:35,601 --> 00:06:38,334
Is there a shorter way?

121
00:06:38,357 --> 00:06:42,357
Taking the path next to the park will get you there quicker.

122
00:06:42,380 --> 00:06:45,213
The path next to the park, got it.

123
00:06:45,236 --> 00:06:49,070
Yes, it’s about a seven-minute walk.

124
00:06:49,093 --> 00:06:51,859
That’s really convenient!

125
00:06:51,882 --> 00:06:54,716
Thank you so much for letting me know.

126
00:06:54,739 --> 00:06:57,339
No problem at all.

127
00:06:57,362 --> 00:07:02,295
If you ever need help with anything, just ask!

128
00:07:02,318 --> 00:07:04,394
I really appreciate it.

129
00:07:04,417 --> 00:07:09,251
I hope the moving work today wasn’t too noisy.

130
00:07:09,274 --> 00:07:11,324
Sorry about that.

131
00:07:11,348 --> 00:07:14,441
Oh no, it was perfectly quiet!

132
00:07:14,464 --> 00:07:16,033
It’s no trouble at all.

133
00:07:16,057 --> 00:07:19,223
I look forward to getting to know you.

134
00:07:19,246 --> 00:07:22,880
Likewise, I’m looking forward to it too.

135
00:07:22,903 --> 00:07:24,403
Scene 4: First Meeting and Business Card Exchange

136
00:07:24,403 --> 00:07:29,603
Nice to meet you. I’m Tanaka from ABC Company.

137
00:07:29,626 --> 00:07:34,468
Nice to meet you. I’m Kimura from XYZ Company.

138
00:07:34,491 --> 00:07:38,858
Thank you for taking the time to meet with me today.

139
00:07:38,881 --> 00:07:43,847
No, thank *you* for coming.

140
00:07:43,870 --> 00:07:46,249
Here’s my business card.

141
00:07:46,272 --> 00:07:48,272
Thank you.

142
00:07:48,295 --> 00:07:51,270
And here’s mine.

143
00:07:51,294 --> 00:07:53,294
Thank you, I’ll take good care of it.

144
00:07:53,317 --> 00:07:57,084
Please, have a seat over there.

145
00:07:57,107 --> 00:07:59,440
Excuse me, thank you.

146
00:07:59,463 --> 00:08:03,629
It’s really hot outside today, isn’t it?

147
00:08:03,652 --> 00:08:07,219
Yes, it’s scorching!

148
00:08:07,242 --> 00:08:10,842
Is your office far from here?

149
00:08:10,866 --> 00:08:15,159
No, it’s near Tokyo Station.

150
00:08:15,182 --> 00:08:18,273
About a fifteen-minute train ride.

151
00:08:18,296 --> 00:08:20,430
That’s close!

152
00:08:20,453 --> 00:08:27,549
Now, about today’s meeting—we’re here to discuss the new website, right?

153
00:08:27,572 --> 00:08:34,744
Yes, we’d like to refresh the design and photos.

154
00:08:34,768 --> 00:08:37,023
Understood.

155
00:08:37,046 --> 00:08:40,324
What kind of design are you looking for?

156
00:08:40,348 --> 00:08:44,218
Something bright and easy to navigate.

157
00:08:44,241 --> 00:08:46,219
Understood.

158
00:08:46,242 --> 00:08:51,676
I’ll prepare a proposal that matches your vision.

159
00:08:51,698 --> 00:08:53,355
Thank you.

160
00:08:53,379 --> 00:08:55,637
Nice to meet you.

161
00:08:55,660 --> 00:09:01,110
Would it be alright if I send it to you by email next Monday?

162
00:09:01,134 --> 00:09:04,111
Yes, that would be great. Thank you.

163
00:09:04,135 --> 00:09:06,535
I'm looking forward to it!

164
00:09:06,558 --> 00:09:09,054
Thank you for your time today.

165
00:09:09,078 --> 00:09:12,559
No, thank *you* for having me.

166
00:09:12,582 --> 00:09:15,000
Excuse me, thank you.

167
00:09:15,024 --> 00:09:16,524
Scene 5: First Conversation in Japanese

168
00:09:16,524 --> 00:09:18,658
Nice to meet you.

169
00:09:18,681 --> 00:09:21,515
Is it alright if I sit here?

170
00:09:21,538 --> 00:09:23,597
Nice to meet you.

171
00:09:23,621 --> 00:09:26,307
Yes, please do.

172
00:09:26,330 --> 00:09:28,226
Thank you.

173
00:09:28,249 --> 00:09:30,983
I'm Kim.

174
00:09:31,006 --> 00:09:33,539
I’m Tanaka.

175
00:09:33,562 --> 00:09:35,979
Nice to meet you.

176
00:09:36,003 --> 00:09:39,693
Nice to meet you. I look forward to getting to know you.

177
00:09:39,717 --> 00:09:43,083
What year are you in, Tanaka?

178
00:09:43,106 --> 00:09:46,282
I'm a sophomore.

179
00:09:46,306 --> 00:09:49,112
What year are you in, Kim?

180
00:09:49,135 --> 00:09:52,554
I'm a freshman.

181
00:09:52,578 --> 00:09:55,345
I came to Japan last month.

182
00:09:55,368 --> 00:09:57,173
I see.

183
00:09:57,196 --> 00:09:59,408
What's your major?

184
00:09:59,431 --> 00:10:01,631
Economics.

185
00:10:01,654 --> 00:10:04,866
What's your major, Tanaka?

186
00:10:04,890 --> 00:10:07,930
I'm also studying economics.

187
00:10:07,954 --> 00:10:10,410
We're in the same department!

188
00:10:10,434 --> 00:10:12,834
Oh, really?

189
00:10:12,857 --> 00:10:14,690
That's great!

190
00:10:14,713 --> 00:10:19,180
Actually, I'm not sure how to register for classes.

191
00:10:19,203 --> 00:10:22,569
Did you pick your classes on the computer?

192
00:10:22,592 --> 00:10:27,826
Yes, I tried, but it was difficult.

193
00:10:27,849 --> 00:10:35,507
You log in through the university website and register for classes from Monday to Friday.

194
00:10:35,530 --> 00:10:37,784
When is the deadline?

195
00:10:37,808 --> 00:10:40,887
This Friday.

196
00:10:40,910 --> 00:10:42,743
Got it.

197
00:10:42,766 --> 00:10:45,700
I'll try doing it tonight.

198
00:10:45,723 --> 00:10:49,923
Feel free to ask me anytime if you're unsure.

199
00:10:49,946 --> 00:10:51,812
Thank you.

200
00:10:51,836 --> 00:10:54,128
That would be a huge help.

201
00:10:54,151 --> 00:10:58,169
By the way, I'm getting hungry.

202
00:10:58,193 --> 00:11:00,126
Yeah, me too.

203
00:11:00,149 --> 00:11:03,282
It's almost lunchtime.

204
00:11:03,305 --> 00:11:06,872
What’s your favorite dish in the cafeteria?

205
00:11:06,895 --> 00:11:10,740
The curry on the first floor is delicious!

206
00:11:10,763 --> 00:11:12,701
Curry, huh?

207
00:11:12,725 --> 00:11:15,258
How much is it?

208
00:11:15,281 --> 00:11:17,615
400 yen.

209
00:11:17,638 --> 00:11:20,513
It's cheap and filling.

210
00:11:20,536 --> 00:11:22,136
Sounds great!

211
00:11:22,159 --> 00:11:25,526
I'll have curry for lunch today.

212
00:11:25,549 --> 00:11:28,635
Shall we go to the cafeteria together?

213
00:11:28,658 --> 00:11:31,125
Yes, I'd love to!

214
00:11:31,148 --> 00:11:34,814
Let's go together after class.

215
00:11:34,837 --> 00:11:37,404
Sure, let's go!

216
00:11:37,427 --> 00:11:38,927
Scene 6: Hair Salon Customer Service and Hairstyle Consultation

217
00:11:38,927 --> 00:11:41,008
Welcome!

218
00:11:41,032 --> 00:11:44,765
Thank you for visiting us today.

219
00:11:44,788 --> 00:11:46,167
Hello.

220
00:11:46,190 --> 00:11:49,524
Nice to meet you. I appreciate your help today.

221
00:11:49,547 --> 00:11:53,113
This is your first time at our salon, right?

222
00:11:53,136 --> 00:11:55,936
Please, have a seat here.

223
00:11:55,959 --> 00:11:59,293
Let me take your belongings for you.

224
00:11:59,316 --> 00:12:01,165
Thank you.

225
00:12:01,188 --> 00:12:03,627
Nice to meet you.

226
00:12:03,651 --> 00:12:07,422
What kind of hairstyle would you like today?

227
00:12:07,445 --> 00:12:11,053
I'd like to go shorter overall.

228
00:12:11,077 --> 00:12:13,416
I want it neat and tidy.

229
00:12:13,440 --> 00:12:15,440
Got it.

230
00:12:15,462 --> 00:12:19,196
Would you like the sides and back trimmed short?

231
00:12:19,219 --> 00:12:22,419
Yes, please keep it short.

232
00:12:22,442 --> 00:12:25,499
Is it okay if I use clippers?

233
00:12:25,522 --> 00:12:28,569
Yes, that's fine.

234
00:12:28,592 --> 00:12:30,592
Understood.

235
00:12:30,615 --> 00:12:33,482
How would you like your bangs?

236
00:12:33,505 --> 00:12:37,105
Please cut them so they don’t touch my eyebrows.

237
00:12:37,128 --> 00:12:38,928
Got it.

238
00:12:38,951 --> 00:12:42,685
Do you usually use styling products?

239
00:12:42,708 --> 00:12:46,554
Yes, I use wax every morning.

240
00:12:46,578 --> 00:12:48,578
Got it.

241
00:12:48,601 --> 00:12:52,267
I’ll cut your hair to make it easier to style.

242
00:12:52,290 --> 00:12:53,973
Thank you.

243
00:12:53,997 --> 00:12:55,674
That would be great, thanks.

244
00:12:55,697 --> 00:12:58,752
Do you have the day off work today?

245
00:12:58,776 --> 00:13:02,853
Yes, I’m off work today.

246
00:13:02,876 --> 00:13:05,876
What do you usually do on your days off?

247
00:13:05,899 --> 00:13:10,187
I take walks in the park or visit cafés.

248
00:13:10,211 --> 00:13:11,977
Sounds great!

249
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:15,835
There’s a great café nearby, by the way.

250
00:13:15,859 --> 00:13:17,713
Really?

251
00:13:17,736 --> 00:13:20,070
I’d love to check it out sometime.

252
00:13:20,093 --> 00:13:23,946
Alright, let’s start with a shampoo.

253
00:13:23,970 --> 00:13:27,703
I’ll show you to the shampoo station.

254
00:13:27,726 --> 00:13:29,859
Of course.

255
00:13:29,882 --> 00:13:32,116
Nice to meet you.

256
00:13:32,139 --> 00:13:33,639
Scene 7: Making a Library Card

257
00:13:33,639 --> 00:13:35,572
Excuse me.

258
00:13:35,595 --> 00:13:38,397
This is my first time here.

259
00:13:38,421 --> 00:13:39,989
Welcome!

260
00:13:40,012 --> 00:13:42,786
Welcome to the library!

261
00:13:42,809 --> 00:13:47,043
I’d like to borrow some books, but I don’t have a card.

262
00:13:47,066 --> 00:13:49,032
Understood.

263
00:13:49,055 --> 00:13:52,033
Let’s make you a library card.

264
00:13:52,057 --> 00:13:54,473
How do I do that?

265
00:13:54,496 --> 00:13:59,031
Please fill in your name and address on this form.

266
00:13:59,055 --> 00:14:00,889
Got it.

267
00:14:00,912 --> 00:14:03,209
I’ll write it here.

268
00:14:03,232 --> 00:14:05,101
Thank you.

269
00:14:05,125 --> 00:14:09,178
Do you have any ID with your address on it?

270
00:14:09,201 --> 00:14:13,001
Yes, I have my residence card.

271
00:14:13,024 --> 00:14:14,881
May I see it?

272
00:14:14,905 --> 00:14:17,556
Yes, I’ve confirmed it.

273
00:14:17,579 --> 00:14:20,146
Here’s your card.

274
00:14:20,169 --> 00:14:22,183
Thank you.

275
00:14:22,206 --> 00:14:25,489
