545
00:28:19,310 --> 00:28:23,643
Please use gloves, tongs, and trash bags.

546
00:28:23,666 --> 00:28:25,266
Thank you.

547
00:28:25,289 --> 00:28:29,022
Do we need to separate the trash?

548
00:28:29,045 --> 00:28:30,522
Yes, it is.

549
00:28:30,546 --> 00:28:35,352
Yes, we’ll sort it into burnable trash, cans, and PET bottles.

550
00:28:35,375 --> 00:28:37,041
Got it.

551
00:28:37,064 --> 00:28:38,998
Got it, I’ll be careful.

552
00:28:39,021 --> 00:28:43,103
The work should take about an hour.

553
00:28:43,127 --> 00:28:46,966
After we’re done, let’s all have some tea together.

554
00:28:46,989 --> 00:28:49,479
I'm looking forward to it!

555
00:28:49,502 --> 00:28:52,599
I'll do my very best today.

556
00:28:52,622 --> 00:28:55,316
Let's do our best together!

557
00:28:55,340 --> 00:28:56,840
Scene 15: Photography Club Entrance / Welcome to the Photography Club

558
00:28:56,840 --> 00:29:01,208
Nice to meet you. Welcome to the Photography Club!

559
00:29:01,231 --> 00:29:02,731
Scene 16: On the Train / Chatting on the Train

560
00:29:02,731 --> 00:29:04,531
Excuse me.

561
00:29:04,554 --> 00:29:07,954
Is this seat 10B?

562
00:29:07,977 --> 00:29:12,156
Yes, that’s the seat next to mine.

563
00:29:12,180 --> 00:29:14,180
Thank you.

564
00:29:14,203 --> 00:29:18,442
I’ll put my luggage on the overhead rack.

565
00:29:18,465 --> 00:29:20,299
Need a hand?

566
00:29:20,322 --> 00:29:22,888
Is your bag heavy?

567
00:29:22,911 --> 00:29:25,511
No, I’ve got it, thanks.

568
00:29:25,534 --> 00:29:28,143
Thanks for asking!

569
00:29:28,167 --> 00:29:31,746
Lovely weather we’re having today, isn’t it?

570
00:29:31,769 --> 00:29:34,206
Where are you headed?

571
00:29:34,230 --> 00:29:37,104
I’m going to Kyoto.

572
00:29:37,127 --> 00:29:40,294
How about you?

573
00:29:40,317 --> 00:29:44,050
I’m getting off at Shin-Osaka.

574
00:29:44,073 --> 00:29:45,507
Are you traveling for fun?

575
00:29:45,530 --> 00:29:47,808
Or is it for work?

576
00:29:47,831 --> 00:29:50,064
Just traveling.

577
00:29:50,087 --> 00:29:52,929
I’m meeting a friend in Kyoto.

578
00:29:52,952 --> 00:29:54,486
Sounds great!

579
00:29:54,510 --> 00:29:58,077
I’m going for work.

580
00:29:58,100 --> 00:30:00,233
Work, huh?

581
00:30:00,256 --> 00:30:02,123
That sounds tough.

582
00:30:02,146 --> 00:30:05,316
Do you go to Kyoto often?

583
00:30:05,339 --> 00:30:08,173
No, it’s been a while.

584
00:30:08,196 --> 00:30:12,529
Kyoto has so many delicious foods!

585
00:30:12,552 --> 00:30:16,847
Matcha ice cream is especially famous.

586
00:30:16,870 --> 00:30:21,044
There’s a great shop near the station.

587
00:30:21,068 --> 00:30:23,406
Matcha ice cream?

588
00:30:23,429 --> 00:30:25,996
I’d love to try it!

589
00:30:26,019 --> 00:30:29,786
Oh, we’re almost in Kyoto.

590
00:30:29,809 --> 00:30:33,079
Thanks for all the tips!

591
00:30:33,102 --> 00:30:36,201
No problem at all.

592
00:30:36,225 --> 00:30:38,916
Hope you have a wonderful trip!

593
00:30:38,939 --> 00:30:41,673
I’m really looking forward to it!

594
00:30:41,696 --> 00:30:44,555
Good luck with your work!

595
00:30:44,578 --> 00:30:46,453
Excuse me.

596
00:30:46,477 --> 00:30:47,974
Thank you.

597
00:30:47,997 --> 00:30:50,874
Take care!

598
00:30:50,897 --> 00:30:52,397
Scene 17: First Conversations / Greetings and Origins

599
00:30:52,397 --> 00:30:54,531
Good evening.

600
00:30:54,553 --> 00:30:57,443
Is it alright if I sit here?

601
00:30:57,467 --> 00:30:59,355
Good evening.

602
00:30:59,378 --> 00:31:01,578
Yes, please do.

603
00:31:01,601 --> 00:31:03,482
Thank you.

604
00:31:03,506 --> 00:31:06,752
This lounge is so beautiful.

605
00:31:06,776 --> 00:31:08,514
Yeah, me too.

606
00:31:08,537 --> 00:31:12,216
It’s so peaceful and relaxing.

607
00:31:12,240 --> 00:31:15,527
Where are you from?

608
00:31:15,550 --> 00:31:18,801
I’m from the U.S.

609
00:31:18,824 --> 00:31:22,102
Where are you from?

610
00:31:22,126 --> 00:31:25,175
I’m from Thailand.

611
00:31:25,199 --> 00:31:28,599
When did you arrive in Japan?

612
00:31:28,622 --> 00:31:31,793
I got here last night.

613
00:31:31,816 --> 00:31:34,673
I’ll be staying for three days.

614
00:31:34,696 --> 00:31:36,496
I see.

615
00:31:36,519 --> 00:31:40,919
I’m staying for four days starting today.

616
00:31:40,942 --> 00:31:43,875
Where did you go today?

617
00:31:43,898 --> 00:31:47,898
I visited a temple nearby.

618
00:31:47,921 --> 00:31:52,455
It was so beautiful at this ancient temple.

619
00:31:52,478 --> 00:31:54,344
Sounds great!

620
00:31:54,367 --> 00:31:58,637
I went shopping near the train station.

621
00:31:58,661 --> 00:32:02,095
Where are you planning to go tomorrow?

622
00:32:02,118 --> 00:32:06,962
Tomorrow, I’m heading to a famous castle first thing in the morning.

623
00:32:06,985 --> 00:32:09,392
Where are you off to?

624
00:32:09,415 --> 00:32:14,828
Tomorrow, I’ll be visiting a big park and an art museum.

625
00:32:14,852 --> 00:32:19,818
There’s a delicious ramen shop near the art museum, by the way!

626
00:32:19,842 --> 00:32:21,775
Really?

627
00:32:21,798 --> 00:32:24,998
I love ramen too!

628
00:32:25,021 --> 00:32:27,233
I’d love to check it out.

629
00:32:27,257 --> 00:32:32,031
Oh, there’s some warm tea over there.

630
00:32:32,054 --> 00:32:34,787
You can have it for free.

631
00:32:34,810 --> 00:32:37,418
That’s great!

632
00:32:37,442 --> 00:32:40,017
Shall I pour you some tea?

633
00:32:40,041 --> 00:32:41,641
Thank you.

634
00:32:41,664 --> 00:32:43,198
Yes, please.

635
00:32:43,221 --> 00:32:45,587
Here you go!

636
00:32:45,610 --> 00:32:48,178
It’s warm green tea.

637
00:32:48,202 --> 00:32:50,018
Thank you.

638
00:32:50,041 --> 00:32:52,850
This tea is so good!

639
00:32:52,873 --> 00:32:57,325
Let’s chat about our travel plans over tea.

640
00:32:57,349 --> 00:33:00,118
Sounds great!

641
00:33:00,141 --> 00:33:01,641
Scene 18: First-Time Hiking Adventure

642
00:33:01,641 --> 00:33:03,721
Good morning.

643
00:33:03,744 --> 00:33:05,811
Nice to meet you.

644
00:33:05,834 --> 00:33:07,838
Good morning.

645
00:33:07,861 --> 00:33:09,676
Nice to meet you.

646
00:33:09,699 --> 00:33:11,784
I’m Tanaka.

647
00:33:11,807 --> 00:33:14,691
I’m Yamada, the hiking club leader.

648
00:33:14,714 --> 00:33:17,548
Nice to meet you. I appreciate your help today.

649
00:33:17,571 --> 00:33:21,371
Nice to meet you. I look forward to getting to know you.

650
00:33:21,394 --> 00:33:24,997
Welcome to the hiking club!

651
00:33:25,020 --> 00:33:29,278
Tanaka, have you been hiking before?

652
00:33:29,302 --> 00:33:32,760
Not much, no.

653
00:33:32,783 --> 00:33:36,383
This is my first time climbing a tall mountain.

654
00:33:36,406 --> 00:33:38,839
Got it.

655
00:33:38,862 --> 00:33:42,343
Today’s mountain is actually quite low.

656
00:33:42,367 --> 00:33:46,500
The trail is easy to walk, so don’t worry.

657
00:33:46,523 --> 00:33:48,656
Great!

658
00:33:48,679 --> 00:33:50,879
That makes me feel a little better.

659
00:33:50,902 --> 00:33:55,036
Let’s check your gear before we head out.

660
00:33:55,059 --> 00:33:58,325
Can I see the shoes you’re wearing?

661
00:33:58,348 --> 00:34:01,395
Sure, these are my shoes.

662
00:34:01,418 --> 00:34:04,785
I wore sturdy sneakers.

663
00:34:04,808 --> 00:34:06,987
Great shoes!

664
00:34:07,011 --> 00:34:10,144
These won’t slip at all.

665
00:34:10,167 --> 00:34:14,181
Do you have rain gear?

666
00:34:14,205 --> 00:34:18,039
Yes, I packed a rain jacket in my backpack.

667
00:34:18,062 --> 00:34:20,229
That's wonderful!

668
00:34:20,252 --> 00:34:24,907
Mountain weather changes quickly, so that’s important.

669
00:34:24,930 --> 00:34:28,597
Do you have enough water or tea?

670
00:34:28,620 --> 00:34:33,620
Yes, I have two 500-milliliter bottles.

671
00:34:33,643 --> 00:34:35,919
That’s plenty.

672
00:34:35,942 --> 00:34:39,362
Did you bring lunch?

673
00:34:39,385 --> 00:34:43,962
Yes, I bought onigiri at a convenience store along the way.

674
00:34:43,985 --> 00:34:47,385
You’re all set!

675
00:34:47,408 --> 00:34:51,842
Today’s route will take about two hours to climb.

676
00:34:51,865 --> 00:34:55,243
Let’s take it slow and rest as we go.

677
00:34:55,266 --> 00:34:59,278
If you get tired at any point, just let me know.

678
00:34:59,302 --> 00:35:01,435
Thank you, I will!

679
00:35:01,458 --> 00:35:04,896
I’ll do my best not to be a bother.

680
00:35:04,920 --> 00:35:07,387
Don’t worry, it’ll be fine.

681
00:35:07,410 --> 00:35:09,743
We’re all here to help each other.

682
00:35:09,766 --> 00:35:13,299
Safety first today!

683
00:35:13,322 --> 00:35:15,941
Alright, let’s get going!

684
00:35:15,965 --> 00:35:19,331
Yes, let’s do this!

685
00:35:19,354 --> 00:35:20,854
Scene 19: First Steps in Pottery – A Beginner’s Journey

686
00:35:20,854 --> 00:35:27,588
Welcome to our pottery class! I’m Yamada, your instructor.

687
00:35:27,611 --> 00:35:31,046
Nice to meet you. I’m Tanaka.

688
00:35:31,069 --> 00:35:33,742
Nice to meet you. I appreciate your help today.

689
00:35:33,766 --> 00:35:36,299
Nice to meet you.

690
00:35:36,322 --> 00:35:40,922
Mr. Tanaka, is this your first time trying pottery?

691
00:35:40,945 --> 00:35:43,813
Yes, it’s my first time.

692
00:35:43,837 --> 00:35:46,804
I’ve always wanted to try it.

693
00:35:46,827 --> 00:35:50,060
That’s wonderful to hear!

694
00:35:50,083 --> 00:35:54,083
What kind of piece would you like to make today?

695
00:35:54,106 --> 00:35:58,473
I’d love to make a rice bowl I can use every day.

696
00:35:58,495 --> 00:36:01,311
A slightly larger one would be perfect.

697
00:36:01,334 --> 00:36:03,101
Sounds great!

698
00:36:03,124 --> 00:36:06,290
Let’s create a beautiful rice bowl together!

699
00:36:06,313 --> 00:36:10,080
First, please wash your hands thoroughly.

700
00:36:10,103 --> 00:36:12,921
I’ve already washed them.

701
00:36:12,944 --> 00:36:16,611
Great! We’ll be using this clay today.

702
00:36:16,634 --> 00:36:20,602
Start by kneading the clay into a smooth ball.

703
00:36:20,626 --> 00:36:22,519
Got it.

704
00:36:22,542 --> 00:36:25,542
I’ll shape it into a round ball with my hands.

705
00:36:25,565 --> 00:36:27,654
You’re doing great!

706
00:36:27,678 --> 00:36:32,445
Next, place it on the pottery wheel.

707
00:36:32,467 --> 00:36:37,909
Wet your hands well, then press the pedal to start the wheel spinning.

708
00:36:37,933 --> 00:36:39,700
Got it.

709
00:36:39,723 --> 00:36:41,889
Okay, my hands are wet now.

710
00:36:41,912 --> 00:36:45,746
Now, use your thumb to make a hole in the center.

711
00:36:45,769 --> 00:36:49,303
Alright, I’ll press gently.

712
00:36:49,326 --> 00:36:52,493
Oh! The hole is forming.

713
00:36:52,516 --> 00:36:54,533
Excellent!

714
00:36:54,556 --> 00:36:59,323
Cradle the clay with both hands and slowly pull it upward.

715
00:36:59,346 --> 00:37:02,622
Got it—I’ll lift it gently.

716
00:37:02,646 --> 00:37:06,525
Wow, it’s starting to look like a rice bowl!

717
00:37:06,548 --> 00:37:09,481
The shape is coming out beautifully.

718
00:37:09,504 --> 00:37:14,560
Flatten the base a bit… and there—it’s done!

719
00:37:14,583 --> 00:37:18,425
How long will it take to be fired and ready?

720
00:37:18,449 --> 00:37:21,548
It usually takes about a month.

721
00:37:21,571 --> 00:37:25,838
Once it’s finished, we’ll deliver it to your home.

722
00:37:25,861 --> 00:37:28,066
I can’t wait!

723
00:37:28,089 --> 00:37:32,538
Thank you so much for guiding me so carefully today.

724
00:37:32,561 --> 00:37:36,295
Not at all—thank *you* for coming!

725
00:37:36,317 --> 00:37:39,613
Feel free to visit anytime.

726
00:37:39,637 --> 00:37:42,331
I’ll definitely be back!